  m_Name: 1968 littering
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Littering Penalties 1968
  info: Singapore introduced anti-littering laws as part of a national campaign to
    maintain a clean and green environment. Fines for littering range from SGD 300
    for small items like cigarette butts to SGD 1,000 for larger offenses. Repeat
    offenders may be subjected to Corrective Work Orders (CWO), requiring them to
    clean public areas while wearing reflective vests, as part of their punishment.
    These public shaming measures serve as both a deterrent and an educational experience.
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 29250f25f4652453e9f5d7a5a19c9110, type: 3}
